eps its current text and it is tried again later.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-landing-pages-and-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Landing pages and guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. A page for a way of renting (monthly, SUV) goes into search once enough real cars match it (Program settings).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. <b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: <b class="gd-ui">Index the place pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the colour pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the search term pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the /buy pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the detailing pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the body shop pages</b>. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Financing disclaimer</b>: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to Bookings &gt; Leads.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Settings: <b class="gd-ui">Index every page</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Only pages that pass the rules</b>: makes, models with 2 or more years of data, years with one of our cars or of a popular model from 2015, trims with one of our cars. The others stay visible but out of search. Also the gas, premium and electricity prices, and how often the catalog is imported (every 30 days).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. <b class="gd-ui">Add trims for another model</b> adds a model that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Catalog import: the last import and its counts. <b class="gd-ui">Import now</b> asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car&#39;s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Quality gate: off. On, only places within the delivery reach are in search, and rental pages only with a real matching car. Search engines can treat many similar pages as low value; the gate lowers that risk.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: every province, state and territory is on. Untick a region to take its pages and sitemaps off the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term (its pages then leave search), switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages say plainly that CarmaCars does not sell, finance or lease cars; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. CarmaCars does not do this work, and the pages say so: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 0123 END
